---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import portraitImage from '../assets/images/maria.webp';
---

<Layout
	title="About | Andrew Smith, UX Design Leader"
	description="Background and approach of Andrew Smith, a UX design leader working across design systems, journey mapping, research operations, and product design."
>
	<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>

	<div class="page">
		<SiteHeader />

		<main id="main-content">
			<section class="hero">
				<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
				<div class="hero-layout">
					<div class="hero-copy">
						<h1 class="display-title">Making the invisible visible, and the complicated usable.</h1>
						<p class="hero-text">
							Design decisions should be won on evidence, not opinion or seniority. That belief
							runs through everything here — from how interfaces get built, to how teams
							decide what to build in the first place.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="hero-portrait-wrap">
						<Image
							class="hero-portrait"
							src={portraitImage}
							alt="Portrait of Andrew Smith"
							loading="eager"
							decoding="async"
							widths={[320, 480, 640]}
							sizes="(max-width: 980px) 100vw, 32vw"
						/>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="editorial-section">
				<div class="section-rail">
					<p class="section-kicker">Background</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-block">
					<p>
						Two decades across front-end development and UX design, including the systems layer
						that sits underneath both: design tokens, component libraries, documentation, and
						the governance that keeps them consistent as a product grows.
					</p>
					<p>
						That range — writing the code, designing the interface, and building the system that
						governs both — is what shapes the approach here. Interfaces are judged not just on
						how they look, but on whether they hold together at scale.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="editorial-section">
				<div class="section-rail">
					<p class="section-kicker">How I Work</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-block">
					<p>
						Start by making the experience visible — journey maps, research, evidence — before
						arguing about solutions. A decision backed by a mapped pain point is a different
						conversation than a decision backed by a hunch.
					</p>
					<p>
						Then build the systems that make good decisions repeatable: design tokens and
						component libraries so consistency doesn't depend on memory, testing cadences so
						validation happens continuously rather than at the end, and documentation that
						outlives any one project.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="editorial-section">
				<div class="section-rail">
					<p class="section-kicker">Focus</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-block">
					<p>
						Particularly interested in the space where UI craft, design systems, and evidence-based
						process meet — products where getting the underlying structure right is what makes
						the interface actually work.
					</p>
					<p>
						See the <a href="/work">craft</a> pages for how this plays out in practice, or the
						<a href="/resume">resume</a> for the leadership track record.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page {
		position: relative;
		width: min(calc(100% - 3rem), 78rem);
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 1.25rem 0 5rem;
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.section-kicker {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		line-height: 1.4;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.hero {
		padding: 6rem 0 4rem;
	}

	.hero-layout {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(15rem, 20rem);
		gap: 2.5rem;
		align-items: start;
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	.hero-copy {
		max-width: 52rem;
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.section-kicker {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--muted-foreground);
		font-style: normal;
	}

	.hero-text,
	.story-block p {
		font-size: 1.08rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.hero-text {
		max-width: 44rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.hero-portrait-wrap {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: flex-end;
		align-self: start;
		padding-top: 0.35rem;
	}

	.hero-portrait {
		width: min(100%, 20rem);
		height: auto;
		display: block;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: 0 18px 40px rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.08);
	}

	.editorial-section {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 16rem minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 2rem;
		padding: 2.5rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.section-rail {
		align-self: start;
	}

	.story-block {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		max-width: 52rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 1100px) {
		.hero-layout {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 1.75rem;
			align-items: start;
		}

		.hero-copy {
			max-width: 100%;
		}

		.hero-text {
			max-width: 42rem;
		}

		.hero-portrait-wrap {
			justify-content: flex-start;
			padding-top: 0;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.page {
			width: min(calc(100% - 1.5rem), 78rem);
			padding-top: 1rem;
		}

		.hero {
			padding: 4rem 0 3rem;
		}

		.editorial-section {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.hero-text,
		.story-block p {
			font-size: 1.05rem;
		}

		.hero-portrait {
			width: min(100%, 16rem);
		}
	}
</style>
